  "body_utf8": "{\"base\": \"main\", \"body\": \"Repaired by `aider` running in a nucleus Firecracker pod (release v2.6.0) on an x86_64 node whose boot is quoted by its TPM (node evidence, ADR 0011).\\n\\n- baseline commit: `9c052db15022a16cc589131efe00e77636de99e4`\\n- repair commit: `9cf5a88825ea48bb7775315742c55a0b4c53b358`\\n- tests in the pod: `Ran 9 tests in 0.001s OK`\\n\\nThe pod holds no forge credential: the host minted a per-call token for the push and for this request, and held both for the operator's approval because they follow model output (a declassification). Evidence for this run is kept by the operator.\", \"head\": \"journey/aider-20261007T020545Z\", \"maintainer_can_modify\": false, \"title\": \"Repair summary.py (aider, nucleus v2.6.0 on a TPM-attested node)\"}",
